1980
01:22:02.580 --> 01:22:04.740
She's like, "We have a fucking wood way treadmill,

1981
01:22:04.740 --> 01:22:05.573
go in the basement."

1982
01:22:05.573 --> 01:22:06.718
I'm like, "I feel like."

1983
01:22:06.718 --> 01:22:07.551
Does it count?

1984
01:22:07.551 --> 01:22:09.240
I don't mind running on the treadmill sometimes,

1985
01:22:09.240 --> 01:22:10.080
but I was like.

1986
01:22:10.080 --> 01:22:12.060
Isn't that how you fucked up your shoulder,

1987
01:22:12.060 --> 01:22:12.930
your knee, or something like that?

1988
01:22:12.930 --> 01:22:13.923
Yes, yes.

1989
01:22:15.420 --> 01:22:18.630
I had a damaged shoulder for years that was just like,

1990
01:22:18.630 --> 01:22:19.860
it bothered me, but not terribly.

1991
01:22:19.860 --> 01:22:21.810
I fell down and like wrenched behind me.

1992
01:22:21.810 --> 01:22:23.670
I mean, I fell so awkwardly as I was like turning

1993
01:22:23.670 --> 01:22:25.590
around a corner, the people in the guard shack

1994
01:22:25.590 --> 01:22:27.187
and where we live must have been like,

1995
01:22:27.187 --> 01:22:28.530
"What is this guy doing?"

1996
01:22:28.530 --> 01:22:29.640
There were no cars, no nothing.

1997
01:22:29.640 --> 01:22:34.413
And I just tore everything, labrum, rotator cuff,

1998
01:22:35.311 --> 01:22:36.457
I had gone and the guy was like,

1999
01:22:36.457 --> 01:22:37.920
"Oh, you need everything fixed."

2000
01:22:37.920 --> 01:22:39.060
And I was like, "All right, we'll do it in April

2001
01:22:39.060 --> 01:22:40.650
after the Boston Marathon."

2002
01:22:40.650 --> 01:22:43.230
And after like a week or so of trying to get through this,

2003
01:22:43.230 --> 01:22:44.063
I just called him I was like,

2004
01:22:44.063 --> 01:22:46.350
"Dude, I can't take it anymore, I come in tomorrow."

2005
01:22:46.350 --> 01:22:47.850
And he was like, it was a Friday,

2006
01:22:47.850 --> 01:22:48.750
he said, "Come in Tuesday."

2007
01:22:48.750 --> 01:22:50.280
And I went in Tuesday, and got it done.

2008
01:22:50.280 --> 01:22:53.700
But to my point about the mindset thing is like,

2009
01:22:53.700 --> 01:22:56.010
if you can just prove to yourself that you can do this,

2010
01:22:56.010 --> 01:22:57.480
get up and run every day for 10 days,

2011
01:22:57.480 --> 01:22:59.970
see if you can get 10 days, 'cause if you get 10,

2012
01:22:59.970 --> 01:23:01.800
20 sounds good too.

2013
01:23:01.800 --> 01:23:04.000
And then the next thing is someone was like,

2014
01:23:05.004 --> 01:23:07.980
I work with a brand called Rona clothing brand.

2015
01:23:07.980 --> 01:23:12.030
They have a 30 day 5K show.

2016
01:23:12.030 --> 01:23:13.470
He's like, yeah, "We're doing this, you wanna do it?"

2017
01:23:13.470 --> 01:23:16.472
I was like, "Yeah, I've been doing it for like five years.

2018
01:23:16.472 --> 01:23:18.870
I'll one up, y'all do 15K."

2019
01:23:18.870 --> 01:23:21.870
Yeah, that's just a subset of what I'm already doing

2020
01:23:21.870 --> 01:23:23.370
every day, and have been forever.

2021
01:23:23.370 --> 01:23:25.800
Yeah, but I think that even that as a starter

2022
01:23:25.800 --> 01:23:28.530
for some people is like, I know Goggins puts up challenges

2023
01:23:28.530 --> 01:23:32.160
all the time, and he's someone that I respect his mindset,

2024
01:23:32.160 --> 01:23:34.740
and I also respect his humility in that like

2025
01:23:34.740 --> 01:23:35.940
he doesn't profess to know everything,

2026
01:23:35.940 --> 01:23:37.200
but he knows what he does know.

2027
01:23:37.200 --> 01:23:38.793
And that's kind of how I feel about the running.

2028
01:23:38.793 --> 01:23:41.040
It's like I know what I know, I'm not the best,

2029
01:23:41.040 --> 01:23:44.803
but I know that you're gonna get my best when I show up,

2030
01:23:44.803 --> 01:23:47.943
we're going, like you're gonna have to kill me to beat me,

2031
01:23:48.870 --> 01:23:50.880
if it comes down to like my choice,

2032
01:23:50.880 --> 01:23:52.443
I'm gonna empty the tank.

2033
01:23:55.170 --> 01:23:58.020
I think that the mindset stuff is you have to prove

2034
01:23:58.020 --> 01:24:00.300
to yourself that you can do it because like you said,

2035
01:24:00.300 --> 01:24:02.760
I have nothing special, I'm every man,

2036
01:24:02.760 --> 01:24:04.440
I'm an average athlete at best,

2037
01:24:04.440 --> 01:24:06.600
I played division three football and hockey.

2038
01:24:06.600 --> 01:24:08.910
I was like, Jack of all trades master of none,

2039
01:24:08.910 --> 01:24:10.680
I was just willing to do whatever I had to do

2040
01:24:10.680 --> 01:24:12.570
to stick around, and be on the team.

2041
01:24:12.570 --> 01:24:15.630
If they needed me to fight, I'll be like, okay, I'll fight.

2042
01:24:15.630 --> 01:24:18.540
But your advantage, or your superpower

2043
01:24:18.540 --> 01:24:19.620
is your mental game.

2044
01:24:19.620 --> 01:24:23.980
Like I hear somebody who really understands

2045
01:24:25.320 --> 01:24:28.440
the idea of non-negotiables, like you're able to commit

2046
01:24:28.440 --> 01:24:31.590
to something, and follow through with action.

2047
01:24:31.590 --> 01:24:35.430
So it's not about VO2 Max or anything like that.

2048
01:24:35.430 --> 01:24:37.110
I couldn't tell you any of those metrics.

2049
01:24:37.110 --> 01:24:38.040
It's it's just about like,

2050
01:24:38.040 --> 01:24:39.407
do you ever wear a heart rate monitor by the way?

2051
01:24:39.407 --> 01:24:40.830
Mh mh.
Like okay.

2052
01:24:40.830 --> 01:24:42.450
Sometimes my watch measures it,

2053
01:24:42.450 --> 01:24:44.880
and it'll put it on Strava, and people will be like,

2054
01:24:44.880 --> 01:24:47.430
dude heart rate of I don't know, 185, blah, blah, blah.

2055
01:24:47.430 --> 01:24:48.870
I'm like, oh, that was my heart rate,

2056
01:24:48.870 --> 01:24:49.770
I didn't even know it was.

2057
01:24:49.770 --> 01:24:52.230
Mario doesn't make you strap one on once in a while?

2058
01:24:52.230 --> 01:24:53.460
That's the best thing about Mario,

2059
01:24:53.460 --> 01:24:56.550
he knows who he is dealing with, he knows his.

2060
01:24:56.550 --> 01:24:58.190
But the point being like,

2061
01:24:59.190 --> 01:25:02.190
that's really like the engine behind all of this,

2062
01:25:02.190 --> 01:25:04.680
is like that mental discipline, and that's a muscle

2063
01:25:04.680 --> 01:25:06.780
just like anything else, that's something you can train,

2064
01:25:06.780 --> 01:25:08.970
just like you can train your running, or your cycling,

2065
01:25:08.970 --> 01:25:10.200
or what have you.

2066
01:25:10.200 --> 01:25:12.060
100%, I wish that that was the one thing

2067
01:25:12.060 --> 01:25:14.430
that people take away from this is that,

2068
01:25:14.430 --> 01:25:16.170
I think of myself as just dopey guy,

2069
01:25:16.170 --> 01:25:18.510
who's made a shitload of mistakes like anyone else.

2070
01:25:18.510 --> 01:25:21.510
Same insecurity, same fear, the difference is

2071
01:25:21.510 --> 01:25:24.420
I'm not letting that control me anymore.

2072
01:25:24.420 --> 01:25:27.540
Fear is such a powerful emotion.

2073
01:25:27.540 --> 01:25:29.100
When I moved to New York City,

2074
01:25:29.100 --> 01:25:31.080
I mean, when I was in high school, it was like,

2075
01:25:31.080 --> 01:25:32.720
my kids asked me the other day, "Dad, did you ever get

2076
01:25:32.720 --> 01:25:34.050
in a fight when you were a kid?"

2077
01:25:34.050 --> 01:25:36.180
I was like, "Did we get into a fight?

2078
01:25:36.180 --> 01:25:38.280
I probably had 200 fights in school."

2079
01:25:38.280 --> 01:25:40.470
And to think about, it is insane,

2080
01:25:40.470 --> 01:25:42.330
'cause there hasn't probably been three fights

2081
01:25:42.330 --> 01:25:44.880
in my kid's school in like the last 10 years.

2082
01:25:44.880 --> 01:25:48.330
But it's just such a different world, but the point is like,

2083
01:25:48.330 --> 01:25:50.610
everyone feels nervous about those kind of interactions,

2084
01:25:50.610 --> 01:25:51.720
but the minute that people think

2085
01:25:51.720 --> 01:25:53.850
you're too nervous to do it, is the minute that

2086
01:25:53.850 --> 01:25:55.440
they'll always want to have a problem with you,

2087
01:25:55.440 --> 01:25:56.880
like classic bully shit.

2088
01:25:56.880 --> 01:26:00.060
So in high school, I realized I'm so afraid of this,

2089
01:26:00.060 --> 01:26:02.220
and this is an ever present danger of growing up

2090
01:26:02.220 --> 01:26:05.280
in this kind of like inner city, like blue collar thing.

2091
01:26:05.280 --> 01:26:06.720
It's like, there's a lot of people dealing

2092
01:26:06.720 --> 01:26:07.590
with a lot of shit.

2093
01:26:07.590 --> 01:26:10.170
And it's like, you don't wanna be the target

2094
01:26:10.170 --> 01:26:11.100
of someone else's shit.

2095
01:26:11.100 --> 01:26:12.690
Like half the kids I was in elementary school

2096
01:26:12.690 --> 01:26:14.070
with were then in the prison.

2097
01:26:14.070 --> 01:26:15.900
So it was like you're with these kids

2098
01:26:15.900 --> 01:26:19.800
who some of them have very difficult households,

2099
01:26:19.800 --> 01:26:22.620
and situations, so you're in this dangerous situation.

2100
01:26:22.620 --> 01:26:23.910
Now, I was just like attack it

2101
01:26:23.910 --> 01:26:26.280
from a very practical standpoint in that I just went

2102
01:26:26.280 --> 01:26:29.220
to the sum boxing club where literally like John Ruiz,

2103
01:26:29.220 --> 01:26:31.350
the heavyweight champion of the world was in there training.

2104
01:26:31.350 --> 01:26:33.720
Boxing gym is like the most intimidating,

2105
01:26:33.720 --> 01:26:35.370
but also the most welcoming place in the world.

2106
01:26:35.370 --> 01:26:36.750
Anyone that has the guts that come in,

2107
01:26:36.750 --> 01:26:39.360
and wants to train, let's go.

2108
01:26:39.360 --> 01:26:40.800
If you approve that, you can come back

2109
01:26:40.800 --> 01:26:43.140
after getting get punched in the face, you're good.

2110
01:26:43.140 --> 01:26:46.320
'Cause that's the ultimate test, is when you get hit back,

2111
01:26:46.320 --> 01:26:47.760
holy shit, do I wanna do this?

2112
01:26:47.760 --> 01:26:50.850
This isn't fun, I can't see, I think my nose is broken,

2113
01:26:50.850 --> 01:26:52.260
and that doesn't take much.

2114
01:26:52.260 --> 01:26:54.450
So I started boxing in high school,

2115
01:26:54.450 --> 01:26:56.670
and scared to death every time, like I said to you,

2116
01:26:56.670 --> 01:26:58.890
when I pulled in here, I was like had that anxiety feeling

2117
01:26:58.890 --> 01:27:01.590
of like, "Oh, I'm gonna spar with this guy who is a killer."

2118
01:27:01.590 --> 01:27:05.730
And it's just similar emotions, the point is that emotion,

2119
01:27:05.730 --> 01:27:09.420
whether it's tied to fear, or telling your story to someone,

2120
01:27:09.420 --> 01:27:12.513
or a big meeting in work, or a speaking gig,

2121
01:27:13.380 --> 01:27:14.700
the emotions are the same.

2122
01:27:14.700 --> 01:27:16.980
If you can learn to deal with those emotions,

2123
01:27:16.980 --> 01:27:19.800
and harness that everyone feels them the same,

2124
01:27:19.800 --> 01:27:22.980
but the people who are successful learn to harness that,

2125
01:27:22.980 --> 01:27:24.480
and use it as their own tool,

2126
01:27:24.480 --> 01:27:27.150
whether it's get them more ready,

2127
01:27:27.150 --> 01:27:29.697
or get them to perform at a higher level,

2128
01:27:29.697 --> 01:27:31.980
and you see it all the time, you don't think that Tom Brady

2129
01:27:31.980 --> 01:27:33.480
is scared to death in the fourth quarter,

2130
01:27:33.480 --> 01:27:35.580
when they're trailing in the Super Bowl?

2131
01:27:35.580 --> 01:27:37.140
The difference is he's feeling the nerves,

2132
01:27:37.140 --> 01:27:39.170
but he's like, let's go, he's using this like.

2133
01:27:39.170 --> 01:27:41.130
Right, you have a strategy to channel that

2134
01:27:41.130 --> 01:27:44.340
into something productive as opposed to letting

2135
01:27:44.340 --> 01:27:45.837
it capsize you.

2136
01:27:45.837 --> 01:27:48.240
And the boxing for me was my outlet

2137
01:27:48.240 --> 01:27:51.030
that I was scared every time I went, every fight,

2138
01:27:51.030 --> 01:27:54.090
every sparring session, but I kept going because

2139
01:27:54.090 --> 01:27:57.470
I don't wanna be controlled by fear, and it served me

2140
01:27:57.470 --> 01:28:00.120
in a lot of ways in life, including dealing with addiction,

2141
01:28:00.120 --> 01:28:02.790
'cause when you're about to go through withdrawals,

2142
01:28:02.790 --> 01:28:06.060
and entering into this like uphill battle that is recovery,

2143
01:28:06.060 --> 01:28:07.800
you're like, I don't wanna do it,

2144
01:28:07.800 --> 01:28:09.500
let me just put it off for a week.

2145
01:28:11.970 --> 01:28:14.370
If you have these tools, you're equipped to deal

2146
01:28:14.370 --> 01:28:16.560
with all these different challenges, and look, it doesn't

2147
01:28:16.560 --> 01:28:21.560
make you immune to mistakes,

2148
01:28:21.870 --> 01:28:23.100
you're gonna make mistakes, but hopefully,

2149
01:28:23.100 --> 01:28:24.480
if you have these mental tools,

2150
01:28:24.480 --> 01:28:26.580
and I think you can continue like you said,

2151
01:28:26.580 --> 01:28:28.710
increase the strength of that mental tool,

2152
01:28:28.710 --> 01:28:31.920
it is mindset by setting realistic goals for yourself,

2153
01:28:31.920 --> 01:28:33.900
and working towards them, maybe it's like I said,

2154
01:28:33.900 --> 01:28:36.300
a mile a day, two miles a day, but the boxing

2155
01:28:36.300 --> 01:28:39.383
was a good analogy for me in that, I just kept doing it,

2156
01:28:39.383 --> 01:28:41.490
and kept dealing 'cause nothing else seemed

2157
01:28:41.490 --> 01:28:44.580
even remotely scary to me as getting in a fight.

2158
01:28:44.580 --> 01:28:47.880
And boxing for the New York Athletic Club, even as an adult,

2159
01:28:47.880 --> 01:28:49.560
I was like, "Man, why am I doing this?

2160
01:28:49.560 --> 01:28:50.520
This is so scary."

2161
01:28:50.520 --> 01:28:51.720
But I'm doing it anyway.

2162
01:28:51.720 --> 01:28:53.083
That's it right there.

2163
01:28:53.083 --> 01:28:56.253
Well, awesome to talk to you, man.

2164
01:28:58.020 --> 01:29:00.600
I trust that like is Berlin the next race

2165
01:29:00.600 --> 01:29:01.433
that you're going for right now?

2166
01:29:01.433 --> 01:29:03.691
Yeah, I'm going to Berlin, September 25th.

2167
01:29:03.691 --> 01:29:05.388
Two weeks later, I'll do Chicago.

2168
01:29:05.388 --> 01:29:06.780
See if I can do a quick turn.

2169
01:29:06.780 --> 01:29:10.650
You make any predictions on Berlin, Chicago double?

2170
01:29:10.650 --> 01:29:11.483
You know what?

2171
01:29:11.483 --> 01:29:15.240
I believe that if you speak your truth,

2172
01:29:15.240 --> 01:29:18.450
and aren't afraid to like say even ambitious goals,

2173
01:29:18.450 --> 01:29:20.130
like, hey, hold me accountable.

2174
01:29:20.130 --> 01:29:23.970
I think that I could run 2:26 there, I think that 2:25,

2175
01:29:23.970 --> 01:29:25.710
I wouldn't be like, "Oh my God, what happened?

2176
01:29:25.710 --> 01:29:27.420
Did I cut the course?"

2177
01:29:27.420 --> 01:29:29.370
2:25 on the right day.

2178
01:29:29.370 --> 01:29:30.780
When I ran 1:10 in Nashville,

2179
01:29:30.780 --> 01:29:33.150
if I feel like that on a marathon course,

2180
01:29:33.150 --> 01:29:36.090
especially like a fast course, I don't think that

2181
01:29:36.090 --> 01:29:37.680
that's unrealistic at all.

2182
01:29:37.680 --> 01:29:42.060
And yeah, I would love to be able to set a new PR

2183
01:29:42.060 --> 01:29:44.550
in the marathon this year at 51.

2184
01:29:44.550 --> 01:29:46.890
And then, like I said, two weeks later, I'll do Chicago.

2185
01:29:46.890 --> 01:29:48.360
I have much lower expectations there,

2186
01:29:48.360 --> 01:29:49.680
I just wanna win my age group.

2187
01:29:49.680 --> 01:29:53.850
And then in March I'll do the final marathon major in Tokyo.

2188
01:29:53.850 --> 01:29:55.410
Wow, wow.

2189
01:29:55.410 --> 01:29:57.240
Seems crazy to me 'cause when I started running,

2190
01:29:57.240 --> 01:29:59.370
I was like, I just wanted to finish the marathon,

2191
01:29:59.370 --> 01:30:00.750
or qualify for Boston.

2192
01:30:00.750 --> 01:30:02.670
And now to look on my bookshelves

2193
01:30:02.670 --> 01:30:03.990
when I have a Zoom call or something,

2194
01:30:03.990 --> 01:30:07.440
and see hardware from Boston, New York, London,

2195
01:30:07.440 --> 01:30:10.620
I'm like, it's so funny because you wanna win this stuff,

2196
01:30:10.620 --> 01:30:12.810
and then you have it, and you're like, next.

2197
01:30:12.810 --> 01:30:14.670
That stuff, it's like I said with the mountain,

2198
01:30:14.670 --> 01:30:16.770
like you get there, and you're like, I climbed Everest,

2199
01:30:16.770 --> 01:30:18.810
I wonder if I can climb every highest peak,

2200
01:30:18.810 --> 01:30:21.030
and whatever like next challenge is.

2201
01:30:21.030 --> 01:30:25.050
I wish that I would do a better job of appreciating

2202
01:30:25.050 --> 01:30:28.890
the process more than I do, and each accomplishment

2203
01:30:28.890 --> 01:30:30.630
a little bit longer as opposed to like,

2204
01:30:30.630 --> 01:30:32.070
all right, what's next?

2205
01:30:32.070 --> 01:30:34.590
We'll build that into your non-negotiables.

2206
01:30:34.590 --> 01:30:36.330
No, you're right, you brought up some really good points

2207
01:30:36.330 --> 01:30:38.125
that I've got a lot of things to reflect on.

2208
01:30:38.125 --> 01:30:39.660
It wasn't my intention there,

2209
01:30:39.660 --> 01:30:40.590
I was just here to have fun with you.

2210
01:30:40.590 --> 01:30:42.120
I've had a great time.

2211
01:30:42.120 --> 01:30:43.481
I'm inspired by everything

2212
01:30:43.481 --> 01:30:46.200
that you're doing, man, I think it's super cool.

2213
01:30:46.200 --> 01:30:49.080
I'm so glad we have this opportunity to sit down together.

2214
01:30:49.080 --> 01:30:51.180
For people that are, are watching or listening,

2215
01:30:51.180 --> 01:30:54.060
check out Ken stuff on Strava, he's for real,

2216
01:30:54.060 --> 01:30:56.400
you can see the paces that he's throwing down,

2217
01:30:56.400 --> 01:30:58.833
He's not fucking around right now.

2218
01:31:00.030 --> 01:31:02.610
And we'll be cheering for you my brother,

2219
01:31:02.610 --> 01:31:05.250
and come back, and share some more with me sometime.

2220
01:31:05.250 --> 01:31:06.160
This has just been fun.

2221
01:31:06.160 --> 01:31:07.170
Yeah, man, next time I come back,

2222
01:31:07.170 --> 01:31:08.910
I've got some crazy prison stories

2223
01:31:08.910 --> 01:31:10.020
that are gonna make your head spin.

2224
01:31:10.020 --> 01:31:12.330
Yeah, all right, we'll just do three hours

2225
01:31:12.330 --> 01:31:13.256
of prison stories.

2226
01:31:13.256 --> 01:31:14.089
(Ken laughs)

2227
01:31:14.089 --> 01:31:15.420
'Cause there is no shortage.

2228
01:31:15.420 --> 01:31:16.380
Thank you for having me, man.

2229
01:31:16.380 --> 01:31:18.030
Honestly, I really appreciate it.

2230
01:31:18.030 --> 01:31:20.880
Congratulations on all your successes, I love it.

2231
01:31:20.880 --> 01:31:24.330
I love seeing people like make a career out of doing things

2232
01:31:24.330 --> 01:31:26.820
that are actually helpful, and make them happy,

2233
01:31:26.820 --> 01:31:29.550
and I'm sure you don't feel like you're working.

2234
01:31:29.550 --> 01:31:31.350
It can feel like work,

2235
01:31:31.350 --> 01:31:32.193
it's still work,

2236
01:31:33.330 --> 01:31:35.850
it's like you prepare for it like you prepare for a race.

2237
01:31:35.850 --> 01:31:38.670
You wanna create the environment for the best experience,

2238
01:31:38.670 --> 01:31:41.430
and that doesn't happen without some effort,

2239
01:31:41.430 --> 01:31:43.753
but mostly joy.

2240
01:31:43.753 --> 01:31:45.900
And it's such a privilege to be able

2241
01:31:45.900 --> 01:31:47.227
to meet people like yourself.

2242
01:31:47.227 --> 01:31:48.993
It certainly comes through.

2243
01:31:50.252 --> 01:31:52.389
It certainly reflects in the show, man, it's awesome.

2244
01:31:52.389 --> 01:31:54.240
And thank you again for having me, I appreciate you.

2245
01:31:54.240 --> 01:31:56.787
Cool, peace.
Peace.

2246
